12.1 Data structure for image time series
In sits, time series are stored in a data frame data structure, both in R and Python. The following code shows the first three lines of a time series containing 1,837 labeled samples of land classes in Mato Grosso state of Brazil. The samples are designated as samples_matogrosso_mod13q1 and are available from package sitsdata. The samples have time series extracted from the MODIS MOD13Q1 product from 2000 to 2016, provided every 16 days at 250 m resolution in the Sinusoidal projection. Based on ground surveys and high-resolution imagery, it includes samples of seven classes: Forest, Cerrado, Pasture, Soy_Fallow, Soy_Cotton, Soy_Corn, and Soy_Millet.


R
Python




# Get the samples from Hugging Face
samples_matogrosso_mod13q1 &lt;- sits_from_hf(
  repo = "e-sensing/samples_book",
  file = "samples_matogrosso_mod13q1.parquet",
  type = "dataset"
)
# Show the first samples
samples_matogrosso_mod13q1[1:4,]

